2. HOW DEPOSIT REFUNDS WORK

  A pre-authorized deposit
  returns to the SAME card
  it was held on - the
  card network routes it
  back along the original
  authorization. There is
  nothing to verify and
  no details to provide:
  the refund's route
  already exists.

  EuroDrive will NEVER:
  - Ask for the deposit
    card's number +
    expiry + a photo of
    the card + a 3D-Secure
    SMS code by email
    ("cross-border
    beneficiary
    verification" is
    invented: the card
    networks do not
    require the payee
    to re-identify the
    card a pre-auth
    already touched -
    a refund runs on
    rails that already
    exist. Card front
    photo + SMS code in
    one email is a
    complete card-fraud
    kit)
  - Set a "90-day
    suspense, then
    8-12 weeks claim"
    deadline (the rental
    terms' 14-day release
    is the only clock;
    deadline pressure
    around a refund you
    are owed is the
    phisher's urgency
    again)
  - Use lookalike
    domains such as
    "eurodrive-refunds"
    or "ed-refund-pay"

